# Anargon's Tablet Tools - settings. Copy this file to .env (same folder, or next to the executable) and fill in
# what you need. .env is never committed (.gitignore). A variable set in the environment wins over .env.
# On GitHub, the CI keys at the bottom are repository VARIABLES instead: Settings > Secrets and variables > Actions >
# Variables (or Secrets, for private links). See README.md, "Configuration".

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- read by the program
# Link to the teardown instructions document (opening the tablet, the update-mode pad, chip recovery). Every recovery
# instruction the program shows points here. Empty: the recovery folder of Anargon-osu/deco640-resources,
# https://github.com/Anargon-osu/deco640-resources/tree/HEAD/recovery
ADT_TEARDOWN_URL=
# Where people are sent for help with a firmware build the tool does not know, and where to go there.
ADT_SUPPORT_URL=https://www.discord.gg/tablet
ADT_SUPPORT_WHERE=Tablet Firmware > Support > Tablet Requests, within the "XPpen Deco 640" thread
# Path to xppen-tools (empty: looked for next to the program and in the current folder).
ADT_XPPEN_TOOLS=
# Folder for the hidden PC-side state (flash count, one-time notes). Empty: %APPDATA%\AnargonsTabletTools on Windows,
# ~/.local/state/AnargonsTabletTools elsewhere.
ADT_STATE_DIR=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- read by build.sh / build.cmd / tests
# Optional source override (empty uses the included ../gd32emu component). The emulator's repository:
# https://github.com/Anargon-osu/GD32EMU
GD32EMU_DIR=
# Stock firmware dumps for tests/run-tests.py. --require-firmware needs February; --require-all-firmware/release CI
# needs both builds. Both must be untouched 64 KB main.bin files (CRC-checked).
# A git repository holding the dumps: tests/run-tests.py clones it into tests/work/dumps-repo/ (and fetches it again
# on later runs). Layout: dumps/<firmware version>/ic902-main.bin, one folder per version, named as the firmware names
# itself (dumps/2025-02-14_release001/ic902-main.bin). Every version there is tested in the digital twin; a new
# version is tested by adding its folder. Without a dumps/ folder each build's dump is picked by CRC. HTTPS only.
# ADT_TEST_DUMPS_REF: a branch, tag or commit to check out (empty: the default branch).
ADT_TEST_DUMPS_REPO=https://github.com/Anargon-osu/deco640-resources
ADT_TEST_DUMPS_REF=
# Or one file per build, which wins over the repository for that build: a local path or an https URL.
ADT_TEST_STOCK_DUMP=
ADT_TEST_STOCK_DUMP_DEC=
# Optional token for a private repository or download link: sent as a header for the git clone (never stored in the
# clone) and as a bearer token for the download links.
ADT_TEST_DUMP_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- GitHub Actions only (repository variables)
# All optional: without them the workflow takes the dumps from Anargon-osu/deco640-resources and the emulator from
# Anargon-osu/GD32EMU, checked against the hash pinned in tests/prepare-emulator.py.
# ADT_TEST_DUMPS_REPO / ADT_TEST_DUMPS_REF   variables: the dumps repository, as above
# ADT_TEST_STOCK_DUMP_URL / ADT_TEST_STOCK_DUMP_DEC_URL   download links for the test dumps (variable or secret)
# ADT_TEST_DUMP_TOKEN    secret: a token that can read the dumps repository or links, if they are private
# GD32EMU_REPO / GD32EMU_REF   variables: the emulator repository (owner/name) and its exact 40-character commit
# GD32EMU_URL / GD32EMU_SHA256   variables: an HTTPS link to gd32emu.cs and its SHA-256
# GD32EMU_TOKEN          secret: a token that can read a private emulator repository (default: ADT_TEST_DUMP_TOKEN)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- tests only
# Stands in for the tablet's flash-count string (USB string 173) in tests/run-tests.py; leave empty in normal use.
ADT_TEST_COUNT_STRING=
